1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,060
you

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,060
you

3
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:43,920
Krishnamurti in dialogue with Dr. Alan W. Anderson. J. Krishnamurti was born in

4
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:49,120
South India and educated in England. For the past 40 years he has been speaking

5
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:54,120
in the United States, Europe, India, Australia, and other parts of the world.

6
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:58,880
From the outset of his life's work he repudiated all connections with

7
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:04,080
organized religions and ideologies and said that his only concern was to set men

8
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:10,520
absolutely unconditionally free. He is the author of many books, among them the

9
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:16,580
Awakening of Intelligence, The Urgency of Change, Freedom from the Known, and The

10
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:22,280
Flight of the Eagle. This is one of a series of dialogues between Krishnamurti

11
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:26,540
and Dr. Alan W. Anderson, who is professor of religious studies at San

12
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:30,900
Diego State University where he teaches Indian and Chinese scriptures and the

13
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:36,980
oracular tradition. Dr. Anderson, a published poet, received his degree from

14
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:41,620
Columbia University and the Union Theological Seminary. He has been honored

15
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:47,660
with a Distinguished Teaching Award from the California State Universities.

16
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:54,900
Mr. Krishnamurti, we were discussing in our conversation last time

17
00:01:55,060 --> 00:02:01,540
meditation, and just as we concluded, you brought up the very beautiful analogy

18
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:10,060
from the flowering of a plant, and it struck me that the order that is

19
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:17,460
intrinsic to the movement of the plant as it flowers is a revelatory image of

20
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:23,460
order that you have been discussing. And we were talking also about the

21
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:29,640
relation of meditation to understanding on the one hand and knowledge on the

22
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:34,780
other, a distinction that's very, very rarely made, though in ordinary language

23
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:40,020
we make the distinction, perhaps unwittingly, it's there, we have the

24
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:45,500
two words, but then to go into what the distinction is was something you were

25
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,380
beginning to do and perhaps we could...

26
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:51,020
K. We can go on.

27
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:57,620
So, we were talking, if I remember rightly, about control.

28
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:59,180
A. Yes.

29
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:03,180
K. And we said the controller is the controlled.

30
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:07,260
And we went into that sufficiently.

31
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:13,860
And when there is control, there is direction.

32
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:18,540
Direction implies will.

33
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:30,700
Control implies will, and in the desire to control there is established a goal

34
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:37,540
and a direction, which means to carry out

35
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:46,460
the decision made by will,

36
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:51,180
and the carrying out is the duration of time.

37
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:51,980
A. Yes.

38
00:03:51,980 --> 00:04:03,860
K. And therefore direction means time, control, will and an end.

39
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:08,980
All that is implied in the word control.

40
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:10,980
Isn't it?

41
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:19,780
So, what place has will in meditation and therefore in life?

42
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,820
A. Yes, yes, yes.

43
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:28,460
K. Or it has no place at all.

44
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:35,060
That means there is no place for decision at all,

45
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:39,460
only seeing, doing.

46
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:45,860
And that doesn't demand will, nor direction.

47
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:49,020
When... You follow?

48
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,580
A. Yes, I do.

49
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:54,380
K. The beauty of this, sir, how it works out.

50
00:04:54,380 --> 00:05:01,380
When the mind sees the futility of control,

51
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:08,100
because it has understood the controller is the controlled,

52
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:11,780
one fragment trying to dominate other fragments,

53
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:19,100
and that the dominant fragment is a part of other fragments,

54
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:25,420
and therefore it is like going round in circles,

55
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:30,220
never, vicious circle, never getting out of it.

56
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:35,900
So, can there be a living without control

57
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:38,300
– just listen to this –

58
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:44,980
without will and without direction?

59
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:48,980
There must be direction in the field of knowledge, agreed,

60
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:54,580
otherwise I couldn't get home, the place I live.

61
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:58,740
I would lose the capacity to drive a car,

62
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:01,380
ride a cycle, speak a language,

63
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:04,700
do all the technological things necessary in life.

64
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:10,060
There, direction, calculation, decision,

65
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:12,900
in that field is necessary.

66
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:15,700
Choice is necessary between this and that.

67
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:22,700
Here, where there is choice, there is confusion,

68
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:26,020
because there is no perception.

69
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:30,500
Where there is perception, there is no choice.

70
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:36,820
Choice exists because the mind is confused between this and that.

71
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:45,340
So, can a life be led without control,

72
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:48,340
without will, without direction?

73
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:51,420
That means time.

74
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:58,740
And that is meditation.

75
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:01,300
Not just a question,

76
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:04,100
an interesting, perhaps a stimulating question,

77
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:07,300
but a question, however stimulating,

78
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:09,460
has no meaning by itself.

79
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:14,500
It has a meaning in living.

80
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:19,020
A. I was thinking about ordinary language usage again,

81
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,460
as you were speaking.

82
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:26,500
It's interesting, isn't it, that when we regard

83
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:31,860
that somebody has performed an action

84
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:36,340
that we call willful,

85
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:38,820
that this is an action that has been undertaken

86
00:07:38,820 --> 00:07:42,660
without understanding.

87
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:47,020
So, in the very distinction between will as a word

88
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:51,140
and willful as an adjective,

89
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:53,900
we have a hint of this distinction.

90
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:57,220
But I'd like to ask you, if I could,

91
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:01,300
about the relationship of will for the moment,

92
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:03,900
even though we're talking about meditation,

93
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:09,780
we did regard that knowledge in its own right

94
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,700
does have a proper career.

95
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:12,580
K. Of course.

96
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:15,540
A. And we say that decision is referred to that,

97
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:18,420
choice is referred to that,

98
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:21,780
and therefore will is operative there.

99
00:08:21,780 --> 00:08:24,340
K. And a direction, everything. A. And a direction, and so on.

100
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:29,420
So we are making a distinction here between

101
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:33,340
will and its role in relation

102
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:37,020
to the whole field of what we call loosely know-how.

103
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:40,620
K. Know-how, knowledge. A. Yes.

104
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:44,700
And the confusion that occurs

105
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:48,940
when that activity, so necessary in its own right,

106
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:52,380
is brought over into this.

107
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:55,180
And then we can't do either of them, really.

108
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:57,340
K. Then we are... That's just what we're explaining.

109
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:01,580
Therefore we become inefficient, personal.

110
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:03,180
A. But you see, we don't think that.

111
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:07,460
What we think is that we can be terribly efficient in knowledge

112
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:10,220
and be what is called unspiritual,

113
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:13,660
and be a success here, and not be a success here,

114
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:16,860
whereas if I understand you correctly,

115
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:22,620
you don't fail in one or the other, you just fail, period.

116
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:27,260
It's a total failure if this confusion is made.

117
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:30,540
You simply can't operate even well here,

118
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,860
no matter what it might look like in the short run.

119
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:40,060
K. As long as you are not completely in order inside yourself.

120
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:42,860
A. Right. Exactly.

121
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:47,420
So the very division that we make between inner and outer

122
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:51,500
is itself a symptom of this terrible...

123
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:54,380
K. ...of thought which has divided the outer and the inner.

124
00:09:54,380 --> 00:10:00,940
A. Yes, yes. I hope you'll bear with me in going through that.

125
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,860
K. Yes, absolutely, you're quite right.

126
00:10:02,860 --> 00:10:08,380
A. I know in religious thought, my academic discipline,

127
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:16,940
in religious thought this confusion, well, the weight of it.

128
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,460
K. I know. A. You feel...

129
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:19,740
K. ...appreciated.

130
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:26,300
And as soon as you begin to make a comment of any kind about it,

131
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:29,020
that is simply raising the question.

132
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:34,940
The extreme rigidity and nervousness that occurs is dramatic.

133
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:35,820
Yes.

134
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:39,020
A. You see, sir, so I'm asking,

135
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:43,180
meditation covers the whole field of living,

136
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:45,020
not one segment of it.

137
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:51,980
Therefore, living a life without control,

138
00:10:51,980 --> 00:11:00,300
without the action of will, decision, direction, achievement.

139
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:01,500
Is that possible?

140
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:07,580
If it is not possible, it is not meditation.

141
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:13,340
Therefore, life becomes superficial, meaningless,

142
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:16,700
and to escape from that meaningless life,

143
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:20,940
we chase all the gurus, the religious entertainments,

144
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:25,260
circuses, you follow, all the practices of meditation.

145
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:29,340
It has no meaning.

146
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,500
Right?

147
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:34,780
A. You know... well, of course you do.

148
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:37,580
It's a rhetorical question.

149
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:42,940
In the classical tradition we have a definition of will.

150
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:48,460
We say that it's desire made reasonable.

151
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:51,180
Now, of course, we've long since lost the idea

152
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:54,380
of what the ancients meant

153
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:57,260
against their contemplative background by the word reason.

154
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:58,860
We think it means calculation,

155
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:01,260
but of course that's not what the classical tradition means

156
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:03,020
when it says reasonable.

157
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:10,060
It points rather to that order which isn't defined.

158
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:13,740
And it occurs to me

159
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:16,140
that if we understood that statement correctly,

160
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:17,900
we'd be saying,

161
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:22,060
will is the focus of desire

162
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:26,060
without my focusing self-consciously.

163
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:27,820
K. Yes, that's right.

164
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:32,780
And watching desire to flower,

165
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:36,380
and therefore watching the will in operation and let it flower,

166
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:40,460
as it flowers, as you are watching it, it dies,

167
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:43,180
it withers away.

168
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:45,020
After all, it's like a flower,

169
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:47,660
you allow it to bloom and it withers.

170
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:49,820
A. It comes to be and passes away in its own...

171
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:54,220
K. Therefore, if you are choicelessly aware

172
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:59,660
of this movement of desire, control, will,

173
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:04,060
focusing that will in action, and so on, so on, so on,

174
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:06,140
let it watch it,

175
00:13:06,140 --> 00:13:12,780
and as you watch it, you'll see how it loses its vitality.

176
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:17,260
So there is no control.

177
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:20,220
So from that arises the next question,

178
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:26,940
which is, direction means space.

179
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:28,060
A. Yes, of course.

180
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:33,980
K. It's very interesting. What is space?

181
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:40,540
Space which thought has created is one thing.

182
00:13:40,540 --> 00:13:47,100
Space that exists in heaven, in our...

183
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:51,420
what is it? In the universe, space.

184
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:55,500
There must be space for a mountain to exist.

185
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:59,500
There must be space for a tree to grow.

186
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:05,900
There must be space for a flower to bloom.

187
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:13,580
So, what is space, and have we space?

188
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:17,820
Or are we all so limited physically

189
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:22,860
to living in a little apartment, little houses,

190
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:26,300
no space at all, outwardly,

191
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:30,380
and therefore having no space, we become more and more violent?

192
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:31,980
A. Yes.

193
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:34,300
K. I don't know if you have watched of an evening

194
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:39,500
when all the swallows are lined up on a vase,

195
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:43,820
and how exact spaces they have in between.

196
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:45,420
You follow, sir?

197
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:50,220
It's marvellous to see that, to see this space.

198
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:53,420
And space is necessary.

199
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,660
And we have no space physically,

200
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:58,460
more and more population, and all the rest of it,

201
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:00,300
and therefore more and more violence,

202
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:03,980
more and more living together in a small flat,

203
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:09,340
a thousand people, crowded, breathing the same air,

204
00:15:09,340 --> 00:15:11,980
thinking the same thing, seeing the same television,

205
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:15,260
seeing the same... reading the same book,

206
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:17,740
going to the same church, believing the same thing.

207
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:21,180
You follow?

208
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:24,940
The same sorrow, the same anxiety, the same fear.

209
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:27,820
My country, all that.

210
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:35,660
So, mind and so the brain has very little space.

211
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:45,900
And space is necessary, otherwise I stifle.

212
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:54,060
So, can the mind have space?

213
00:15:55,900 --> 00:16:01,180
And there will be no space if there is a direction.

214
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:03,100
A.S. – Clearly, yes.

215
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,940
K. – You see, sir? A.S. – Of course.

216
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:06,620
A.S. – Yes, I do.

217
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:11,980
K. – There is no space if direction means time.

218
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:22,540
And when the mind is occupied

219
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:27,180
with family, with business, with God, with drink, with sex,

220
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:34,460
with experience, occupied, filled, there is no space.

221
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:38,940
A.S. – That's right. Exactly.

222
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:47,340
K. – So, when knowledge occupies the whole field of the mind as thought,

223
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:50,860
there is no space.

224
00:16:53,100 --> 00:17:00,060
And thought creates space round itself,

225
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:09,020
as the me enclosed and you enclosed, we and they.

226
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:15,100
So, the self, the me, which is the very essence of thought,

227
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:19,340
has its own little space.

228
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:29,980
And to move out of that space is terror, is fear, is anxiety,

229
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:36,060
because I am only used to that little space.

230
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:40,300
A.S. – Yes, exactly.

231
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:42,940
That brings us back to the earlier conversation we had

232
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:45,100
when we touched the point of terror.

233
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:47,340
K. – Yes, that's right.

234
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:50,460
The not-being,

235
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:56,620
and the being is in the little space which thought has created.

236
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:02,220
So thought can never give space.

237
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:06,140
A.S. – Of course not.

238
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:12,300
So, meditation is the freedom,

239
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:18,220
is the freeing of the mind, of its content as consciousness,

240
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:22,460
which creates its own little space.

241
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:27,740
You follow, sir? A.S. – Yes, I do.

242
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:33,340
K. – So, from that it says, is that possible?

243
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:37,980
Because I am occupied with my wife, my children, my responsibilities,

244
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:40,620
I care for the tree, I care for the cat,

245
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:48,140
I care for this and that, and I am occupied, occupied, occupied.

246
00:18:48,140 --> 00:18:53,420
A.S. – This throws a marvellous light on that saying of Jesus,

247
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:56,620
which people have pondered and wondered about,

248
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:59,900
and thought is very strange.

249
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:03,100
Foxes have holes and the birds of the air have nests,

250
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:07,580
but the son of man hath not where to lay his head.

251
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:16,220
He doesn't... man as such, who grasps himself, understands,

252
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:24,140
is not inventing a space for himself.

253
00:19:25,260 --> 00:19:29,180
It fits perfectly, it fits perfectly. That's marvellous.

254
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,100
K. – I don't know what... A.S. – No, I understand,

255
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:33,820
but I was thinking in a context of the whole discourse.

256
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:36,700
It just flashed over me.

257
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:42,380
Our conversations have been such a revelation to me

258
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:47,500
with respect to the literatures that I've soaked myself in for so many years.

259
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:52,940
And it's a demonstration to me of what you've said, for instance,

260
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:59,420
insofar as I ask these questions of myself personally,

261
00:20:01,820 --> 00:20:05,180
precisely as they become answered.

262
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:09,420
So all these things out here become answered.

263
00:20:09,420 --> 00:20:13,420
And what could be more empirically demonstrable to an individual

264
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:16,620
that I am the world and the world is me, than that?

265
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:20,940
So all I'm doing is just giving a report on the journey

266
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:22,060
without direction.

267
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:28,860
K. Sir, look, as the world is getting more and more overpopulated,

268
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:31,900
cities are going more and more, spreading, spreading, spreading,

269
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:37,820
suburbs and so on, man is getting less and less space,

270
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:41,580
therefore driving out animals, killing – you follow this question? –

271
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:44,700
killing the American Indians,

272
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:47,740
killing the Indians in Brazil and so on.

273
00:20:47,740 --> 00:20:49,740
They are doing this, actually going on.

274
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:52,060
A. Oh, yes.

275
00:20:53,020 --> 00:21:01,420
And having no space out there, outwardly,

276
00:21:01,420 --> 00:21:06,700
except on occasions I go often to the country and say,

277
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:08,860
oh my God, I wish I could live here,

278
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:12,380
but I can't because I've got... and so on.

279
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:17,340
So can there be space inwardly?

280
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:20,860
When there is space inwardly, there is space outwardly.

281
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:22,620
A. Exactly.

282
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:28,060
K. But the outward space is not going to give the inner space.

283
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:32,940
The inner space of mind that is free from occupation,

284
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:36,700
though it is occupied at the moment,

285
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:39,420
with what it has to do, it is occupied,

286
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:43,020
but the moment it finishes, it's over.

287
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:48,380
I don't carry the office to my home.

288
00:21:48,380 --> 00:21:51,180
It's over.

289
00:21:51,180 --> 00:22:00,220
So, space in the mind means the emptying of consciousness

290
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:02,300
of all its content,

291
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:04,940
and therefore the consciousness

292
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:08,380
which thought as the me has created ends,

293
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:11,980
and therefore there is space.

294
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:17,900
And that space isn't yours or mine, it's space.

295
00:22:21,020 --> 00:22:27,660
A. Yes, I was thinking of the creation story in Genesis.

296
00:22:27,660 --> 00:22:30,620
The appearance of space occurs

297
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:38,380
when the waters are separated from the waters,

298
00:22:38,540 --> 00:22:45,020
and we have the vault now over which the birds fly,

299
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:50,220
and this space is called heaven.

300
00:22:52,220 --> 00:22:53,260
And in the context of...

301
00:22:53,260 --> 00:22:54,700
K. It is heaven. A. It is heaven.

302
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:58,300
K. That's right. A. Yes, yes, of course.

303
00:22:58,300 --> 00:23:01,260
But then we read that, you see, and we don't...

304
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:04,780
K. Fortunately I don't read any of those things.

305
00:23:04,780 --> 00:23:06,140
You follow?

306
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:14,780
Goodness! So, space, direction, time, will,

307
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:18,860
choice, control. You understand, sir?

308
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:26,540
Now, all that has importance in my living,

309
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:31,180
in the daily living of my life, of every human being.

310
00:23:31,180 --> 00:23:34,540
If he doesn't know the meaning of meditation,

311
00:23:34,540 --> 00:23:38,220
he merely lives in that field of knowledge,

312
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:40,780
and therefore that becomes a prison.

313
00:23:40,780 --> 00:23:42,780
And therefore being a prison, he says,

314
00:23:42,780 --> 00:23:44,780
I must escape through entertainment,

315
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:48,140
through gods, through this and through that, through amusement.

316
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:50,780
You know, that's what is actually taking place.

317
00:23:50,780 --> 00:23:54,620
A. The word vacation... K. Vacation, that's right.

318
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:57,900
A. ...says it all, doesn't it? K. Yes, absolutely.

319
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:01,580
A. To vacate is to exit into... K. ...space.

320
00:24:01,580 --> 00:24:03,580
Space.

321
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:09,340
A. But then we go from one hole to another.

322
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:11,500
K. Another hole.

323
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:17,820
Now, if that is clearly established, perceived in myself,

324
00:24:17,820 --> 00:24:22,540
I see the thing operating in my daily life,

325
00:24:22,540 --> 00:24:24,860
then what takes place?

326
00:24:24,860 --> 00:24:28,140
Space means silence.

327
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:34,380
If there is no silence, it's direction.

328
00:24:35,260 --> 00:24:37,740
It's the operation of, I must do, I must not do,

329
00:24:37,740 --> 00:24:41,980
I must practise this, I must get this. You follow?

330
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:44,780
This should be, should not be, what has been,

331
00:24:44,780 --> 00:24:49,100
should not be, I regret, all that operates.

332
00:24:49,100 --> 00:24:54,700
Therefore, space means silence, inwardly.

333
00:24:55,660 --> 00:25:01,020
A. That's very deep, very, very deep.

334
00:25:01,020 --> 00:25:07,180
It... archetypally we associate manifestation

335
00:25:07,180 --> 00:25:10,620
as over against latency with sound.

336
00:25:10,620 --> 00:25:12,940
K. Yes, sound.

337
00:25:12,940 --> 00:25:18,540
A. And what you said puts the whole thing into an astonishing perspective.

338
00:25:18,540 --> 00:25:24,140
K. Silence isn't the space between two noises.

339
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:31,820
Silence isn't the cessation of noise.

340
00:25:31,820 --> 00:25:38,300
Silence isn't something that thought has created.

341
00:25:38,300 --> 00:25:44,300
It comes naturally, inevitably, as you open,

342
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:48,380
as you observe, as you examine, as you investigate.

343
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:51,820
So, then the question arises,

344
00:25:51,820 --> 00:25:56,940
silence without a movement,

345
00:25:56,940 --> 00:25:59,340
movement of direction, movement of thought,

346
00:25:59,340 --> 00:26:02,940
movement of time, or silence.

347
00:26:02,940 --> 00:26:09,740
Now, that silence, can that operate in my daily life?

348
00:26:13,820 --> 00:26:18,460
I live in the field of noise as knowledge.

349
00:26:19,420 --> 00:26:22,940
That I have to do.

350
00:26:22,940 --> 00:26:27,580
And can I... is there a living with silence,

351
00:26:27,580 --> 00:26:31,340
and at the same time the other?

352
00:26:31,340 --> 00:26:36,300
The two moving together, two rivers flowing,

353
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:39,740
in balance, not division, you follow?

354
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:44,460
In harmony there is no division. Is that possible?

355
00:26:44,460 --> 00:26:47,100
Because otherwise, if that's not possible,

356
00:26:48,060 --> 00:26:52,540
to be deeply honest, I can only live there,

357
00:26:52,540 --> 00:26:55,500
in the field of knowledge. I don't know if you...

358
00:26:55,500 --> 00:26:57,420
A. Oh, yes, yes.

359
00:26:57,420 --> 00:27:01,820
K. So, for me it is possible,

360
00:27:01,820 --> 00:27:03,980
therefore I am not saying out of vanity,

361
00:27:03,980 --> 00:27:08,700
I say this in great humility, I say that is possible, it is so.

362
00:27:08,700 --> 00:27:12,700
Then what takes place?

363
00:27:12,940 --> 00:27:16,540
Then what is creation?

364
00:27:18,940 --> 00:27:23,340
Is creation something to be expressed,

365
00:27:23,340 --> 00:27:26,460
in painting, in poem, in statue, in writing,

366
00:27:26,460 --> 00:27:33,340
in bringing about a baby, is that creation?

367
00:27:34,220 --> 00:27:42,060
Does creation need... or must it be expressed?

368
00:27:42,060 --> 00:27:46,380
To us it must be expressed, to most people.

369
00:27:46,380 --> 00:27:49,660
Otherwise one feels frustrated, anxious,

370
00:27:49,660 --> 00:27:53,020
I am not living, you follow? All that.

371
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:56,460
So what is creation?

372
00:28:01,820 --> 00:28:05,820
One can only answer that if one has really gone through all this.

373
00:28:05,820 --> 00:28:08,300
You understand, sir?

374
00:28:08,300 --> 00:28:12,860
Otherwise creation becomes a rather cheap thing.

375
00:28:12,860 --> 00:28:15,980
A. Yes, it becomes, in terms of the word expressed,

376
00:28:15,980 --> 00:28:18,380
simply something pressed out. K. Pressed out, of course.

377
00:28:18,380 --> 00:28:20,140
A. That's all. K. At all.

378
00:28:20,140 --> 00:28:23,980
Like the writer, literary people, some of them,

379
00:28:23,980 --> 00:28:28,860
are everlastingly in battle in themselves with tension,

380
00:28:28,860 --> 00:28:33,500
and out of that they write a book, become famous.

381
00:28:33,500 --> 00:28:35,740
A. Yes, the psychological theory that works of art

382
00:28:35,740 --> 00:28:39,820
is based on neurosis, which means I am driven.

383
00:28:39,820 --> 00:28:44,460
K. Yes. So what is creation?

384
00:28:53,260 --> 00:28:56,380
Is it something,

385
00:28:57,340 --> 00:29:02,860
a flowering in which the flower does not know

386
00:29:02,860 --> 00:29:06,780
that it is flowering?

387
00:29:06,780 --> 00:29:09,900
I don't... A. Exactly. Exactly.

388
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:14,060
K. Have I made it clear? A. Yes, you have made it very, very clear.

389
00:29:14,060 --> 00:29:20,220
All through our conversations, the one word that has, for me,

390
00:29:20,780 --> 00:29:25,900
being like the clean blade of a two-edged sword,

391
00:29:25,900 --> 00:29:30,620
has been this word, act.

392
00:29:30,780 --> 00:29:37,420
But not act over against inaction.

393
00:29:37,420 --> 00:29:39,020
K. No, no, no, no.

394
00:29:39,020 --> 00:29:42,780
A. Not action as over against

395
00:29:42,780 --> 00:29:45,820
the philosophical term of its opposite, passion,

396
00:29:45,820 --> 00:29:47,420
which is a different use from the one

397
00:29:47,420 --> 00:29:51,100
that you were using in our conversations.

398
00:29:51,100 --> 00:29:56,380
But sheerly act.

399
00:29:56,380 --> 00:29:59,260
Sheerly act.

400
00:29:59,260 --> 00:30:04,220
So, sir, see what takes place.

401
00:30:04,460 --> 00:30:08,780
Creation in my living.

402
00:30:10,700 --> 00:30:11,580
You follow, sir?

403
00:30:11,580 --> 00:30:16,380
Not expressing, creating a beautiful chair, this or that,

404
00:30:16,380 --> 00:30:22,700
that may come, that will come, but in living.

405
00:30:24,700 --> 00:30:27,660
And from that arises another question,

406
00:30:27,660 --> 00:30:32,220
which is really much more important.

407
00:30:32,860 --> 00:30:36,780
Thought is measure.

408
00:30:37,500 --> 00:30:43,420
And as long as we cultivate thought,

409
00:30:44,700 --> 00:30:49,500
and all our actions based on thought, as it is now,

410
00:30:50,620 --> 00:30:55,340
the search for the immeasurable has no meaning.

411
00:30:57,900 --> 00:31:02,300
I can give a meaning to it, say, there is the immeasurable,

412
00:31:02,300 --> 00:31:06,620
there is the unnameable, there is the eternal,

413
00:31:06,620 --> 00:31:09,260
don't let us talk about it, it is there.

414
00:31:09,260 --> 00:31:11,980
It has no meaning.

415
00:31:11,980 --> 00:31:15,100
That is just a supposition, a speculation,

416
00:31:15,100 --> 00:31:19,980
or the assertion of a few who think they know.

417
00:31:19,980 --> 00:31:22,700
One has discarded all that.

418
00:31:22,700 --> 00:31:25,980
Therefore, I ask,

419
00:31:25,980 --> 00:31:30,540
when the mind is utterly silent,

420
00:31:31,740 --> 00:31:34,940
what is the immeasurable?

421
00:31:34,940 --> 00:31:36,140
You follow, sir?

422
00:31:36,140 --> 00:31:41,740
What is the everlasting, what is the eternal?

423
00:31:41,740 --> 00:31:45,740
Not in terms of God, you know, all these things man has invented,

424
00:31:45,740 --> 00:31:51,980
actually to be that.

425
00:31:52,860 --> 00:31:56,380
I don't know if you understand.

426
00:31:59,020 --> 00:32:07,180
Now, silence in that deep sense of that word opens the door,

427
00:32:07,180 --> 00:32:11,420
because you have got there all your energy,

428
00:32:11,420 --> 00:32:14,940
not a thing is wasted,

429
00:32:14,940 --> 00:32:20,620
there is no dissipation of energy at all.

430
00:32:20,620 --> 00:32:26,220
Therefore, in that silence there is summation of energy.

431
00:32:26,220 --> 00:32:28,380
A. Precisely.

432
00:32:28,380 --> 00:32:33,420
K. Not stimulated energy, not self-projected energy, and so on,

433
00:32:33,420 --> 00:32:36,860
that's all too childish.

434
00:32:36,860 --> 00:32:40,620
Because there is no conflict,

435
00:32:41,420 --> 00:32:45,420
no control,

436
00:32:45,420 --> 00:32:50,140
no reaching out or not reaching,

437
00:32:52,620 --> 00:32:57,980
searching, asking, questioning, demanding, waiting, praying,

438
00:32:57,980 --> 00:33:00,620
none of that.

439
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:04,780
Therefore, there is tremendous...

440
00:33:04,780 --> 00:33:07,420
all that energy which has been wasted

441
00:33:07,420 --> 00:33:12,460
is now gathered in that silence.

442
00:33:12,860 --> 00:33:14,140
Do you understand?

443
00:33:14,140 --> 00:33:18,140
That silence has become sacred,

444
00:33:18,140 --> 00:33:19,820
because obviously...

445
00:33:19,820 --> 00:33:20,780
A. Of course it has.

446
00:33:20,780 --> 00:33:24,220
K. It has not the sacred thing which thought has invented.

447
00:33:24,220 --> 00:33:26,140
A. No, not the sacred over against the prophet.

448
00:33:26,140 --> 00:33:27,740
K. No, no, no, all that kind of stuff.

449
00:33:27,740 --> 00:33:28,940
A. No, no.

450
00:33:28,940 --> 00:33:33,340
K. So, it is only such a sacred mind

451
00:33:33,340 --> 00:33:38,700
can see the most supreme sacred,

452
00:33:38,700 --> 00:33:41,900
the essence of all that is sacred, which is beauty.

453
00:33:41,900 --> 00:33:43,980
You follow, sir? A. I do.

454
00:33:43,980 --> 00:33:46,540
K. So, there it is.

455
00:33:46,540 --> 00:33:51,580
God isn't something that man has invented,

456
00:33:51,580 --> 00:33:57,260
or created it out of his image and longing and failure,

457
00:33:57,260 --> 00:34:04,460
but when the mind itself becomes sacred,

458
00:34:04,460 --> 00:34:09,420
then it opens the door to something that is immeasurably sacred.

459
00:34:09,420 --> 00:34:12,380
That is religion.

460
00:34:12,380 --> 00:34:17,980
And that affects the daily living,

461
00:34:17,980 --> 00:34:20,940
the way I talk, the way I treat people,

462
00:34:20,940 --> 00:34:26,860
the conduct, behaviour, all that.

463
00:34:26,860 --> 00:34:30,380
That is the religious life.

464
00:34:30,380 --> 00:34:38,140
If that doesn't exist, then every other mischief will exist,

465
00:34:38,140 --> 00:34:43,340
however clever, however intelligent, however all that.

466
00:34:43,340 --> 00:34:49,020
A. And meditation does not occur

467
00:34:49,020 --> 00:34:51,900
in the context of all this disorder.

468
00:34:51,900 --> 00:34:53,100
Absolutely not.

469
00:34:53,100 --> 00:34:58,300
But in its ongoingness, the way you have mentioned it,

470
00:34:58,300 --> 00:35:02,620
one is precisely in that,

471
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:05,340
you see...

472
00:35:05,340 --> 00:35:11,660
A. Where what your word, religious, is pointing to.

473
00:35:11,660 --> 00:35:14,780
K. That's the most profound religious way of living.

474
00:35:14,780 --> 00:35:18,540
See, sir, what takes place, another thing.

475
00:35:18,540 --> 00:35:21,340
See, as this thing is happening,

476
00:35:21,340 --> 00:35:26,060
because your energy is being gathered,

477
00:35:26,060 --> 00:35:29,260
energy is being gathered, not your energy is being gathered,

478
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:34,380
you have other kinds of powers, extra-sensory power,

479
00:35:34,380 --> 00:35:37,740
you can do miracles, it has happened all this to me,

480
00:35:37,740 --> 00:35:43,100
exercise, that kind of stuff, healing,

481
00:35:43,100 --> 00:35:50,460
but they become totally irrelevant.

482
00:35:50,460 --> 00:35:52,140
Not that you don't love people,

483
00:35:52,140 --> 00:35:55,740
on the contrary, religion is the essence of it,

484
00:35:55,740 --> 00:36:00,060
but they are all secondary issues.

485
00:36:00,060 --> 00:36:05,980
And people get caught in the secondary issues.

486
00:36:05,980 --> 00:36:07,340
I mean, look what is happening.

487
00:36:07,340 --> 00:36:11,660
A man who really can heal, he becomes...

488
00:36:12,860 --> 00:36:19,260
I have people who worship him, a little healing.

489
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:22,540
A. It reminds me of a story you told me once,

490
00:36:22,540 --> 00:36:32,780
I think it was a year ago, when it was about the

491
00:36:32,780 --> 00:36:35,500
old man sitting on the banks of the river,

492
00:36:35,500 --> 00:36:39,900
and the young man came to him,

493
00:36:39,900 --> 00:36:43,500
after the older man had sent him away,

494
00:36:43,500 --> 00:36:46,300
to undertake whatever he needed to learn and all this,

495
00:36:46,300 --> 00:36:48,300
and he came back with a marvellous announcement

496
00:36:48,300 --> 00:36:50,940
that he could now walk on water,

497
00:36:51,580 --> 00:36:56,140
and you said that the older man looked at him and said,

498
00:36:56,140 --> 00:36:59,820
what's all that about, so you can walk on water?

499
00:36:59,820 --> 00:37:02,860
And you have taken all these years to learn how to walk on water.

500
00:37:02,860 --> 00:37:05,740
Didn't you see the boat over there?

501
00:37:05,740 --> 00:37:07,980
That's right, sir.

502
00:37:07,980 --> 00:37:11,100
Of course, of course.

503
00:37:11,100 --> 00:37:14,780
You see, sir, it is very important,

504
00:37:14,780 --> 00:37:17,980
when there is this...

505
00:37:17,980 --> 00:37:19,740
Religion is, as we said,

506
00:37:19,740 --> 00:37:26,140
is the gathering of all energy, which is attention.

507
00:37:26,140 --> 00:37:29,980
In that attention many things happen.

508
00:37:29,980 --> 00:37:36,220
Some of them have this gift of healing, miracles.

509
00:37:36,220 --> 00:37:39,580
I've had it, and I know of which I am speaking about.

510
00:37:39,580 --> 00:37:45,500
And religious man never touches it. You follow?

511
00:37:45,500 --> 00:37:47,660
He may say occasionally, do this or that,

512
00:37:47,660 --> 00:37:53,740
but it is a thing to be put away,

513
00:37:53,740 --> 00:37:56,140
like a gift, like a talent,

514
00:37:56,140 --> 00:38:01,020
it is to be put away because it is a danger.

515
00:38:01,020 --> 00:38:02,300
A. Exactly.

516
00:38:02,300 --> 00:38:06,460
K. The more your talent, the more me.

517
00:38:06,460 --> 00:38:10,380
I am important, I have this talent, worship me.

518
00:38:10,380 --> 00:38:17,020
With that talent I get money, position, power.

519
00:38:17,020 --> 00:38:21,420
So this too is a most dangerous thing.

520
00:38:21,420 --> 00:38:28,940
So a mind that is religious is aware of all this,

521
00:38:28,940 --> 00:38:36,060
and lives a life in this space, in this marvellous space.

522
00:38:36,060 --> 00:38:43,420
Something occurred to me about our discussion earlier

523
00:38:43,420 --> 00:38:45,260
concerning energy,

524
00:38:45,260 --> 00:38:55,180
and your remark that energy, when it patterns itself...

525
00:38:55,180 --> 00:39:00,620
I've forgotten what you used to designate

526
00:39:00,620 --> 00:39:02,300
what the patterned energy was,

527
00:39:02,300 --> 00:39:05,660
but I suspect it's what we often call matter.

528
00:39:05,660 --> 00:39:09,500
Who wouldn't that be correct? Right.

529
00:39:09,660 --> 00:39:16,300
In terms of this pointing to act that you have mentioned,

530
00:39:16,300 --> 00:39:21,900
it throws a very, very different light

531
00:39:21,900 --> 00:39:27,180
on the character of patterned energy,

532
00:39:27,180 --> 00:39:32,700
and draws our gaze away from the pattern,

533
00:39:32,700 --> 00:39:38,940
and reminds us that the substance,

534
00:39:38,940 --> 00:39:42,780
or rather the substantive element

535
00:39:42,780 --> 00:39:44,460
– I don't want to use the word substance there

536
00:39:44,460 --> 00:39:45,980
for philosophical reasons –

537
00:39:45,980 --> 00:39:48,940
the substantive element that we point to

538
00:39:48,940 --> 00:39:50,700
is not the pattern, but the energy.

539
00:39:50,700 --> 00:39:51,820
K. Energy, quite.

540
00:39:51,820 --> 00:39:56,860
You see, sir, that is love, isn't it, sir?

541
00:39:56,860 --> 00:40:02,140
When there is this sense of religious summation of energy,

542
00:40:02,140 --> 00:40:04,700
that is love, that's compassion,

543
00:40:04,700 --> 00:40:09,340
and care, that operates in daily life.

544
00:40:09,340 --> 00:40:13,980
A. In love, the pattern never resists change.

545
00:40:13,980 --> 00:40:18,300
K. So, you see, sir, that love, you can do what you like,

546
00:40:18,300 --> 00:40:21,660
it will be still love.

547
00:40:21,660 --> 00:40:28,940
But there the love becomes sensation.

548
00:40:28,940 --> 00:40:30,620
You follow? A. Yes, yes.

549
00:40:30,620 --> 00:40:33,420
On the whole track of knowledge.

550
00:40:33,420 --> 00:40:36,860
K. And therefore there is no love there.

551
00:40:39,660 --> 00:40:42,700
A. Yes, that image of the lion on the train,

552
00:40:42,700 --> 00:40:46,940
the toy that goes round and round,

553
00:40:46,940 --> 00:40:50,060
isn't that extraordinary?

554
00:40:50,060 --> 00:40:55,100
K. You see, sir, that means, can the mind

555
00:40:55,100 --> 00:40:57,260
– I am using the word mind,

556
00:40:57,260 --> 00:41:01,660
in the sense, mind, the brain, the body, the whole thing –

557
00:41:01,660 --> 00:41:07,260
can the mind be really silent?

558
00:41:08,300 --> 00:41:14,860
Not induced silence, not silence put together,

559
00:41:14,860 --> 00:41:20,140
not silence that thought imagines is silence,

560
00:41:21,100 --> 00:41:25,180
not the silence of a church or the temple.

561
00:41:25,180 --> 00:41:26,460
They have their own silence.

562
00:41:26,460 --> 00:41:30,620
When you enter a temple or an old cathedral,

563
00:41:30,620 --> 00:41:33,180
they have an extraordinary sense of silence.

564
00:41:33,180 --> 00:41:37,260
Thousands of people chanted, talked, prayed, all that,

565
00:41:37,260 --> 00:41:40,860
but it is above all that.

566
00:41:40,860 --> 00:41:44,220
It is not that either.

567
00:41:45,580 --> 00:41:52,220
So, this silence isn't contrived,

568
00:41:52,860 --> 00:41:55,820
and therefore it is real.

569
00:41:55,820 --> 00:42:01,420
It isn't, I have brought about through practice, a silence.

570
00:42:01,820 --> 00:42:03,420
A. No, it's not what you mentioned earlier,

571
00:42:03,420 --> 00:42:06,300
that space between two noises,

572
00:42:06,300 --> 00:42:08,380
because that would become an interval.

573
00:42:08,380 --> 00:42:09,180
K. Yes, that's right.

574
00:42:09,180 --> 00:42:11,980
A. And as an interval it simply becomes successive.

575
00:42:11,980 --> 00:42:15,100
K. Successive. That's right.

576
00:42:15,740 --> 00:42:17,740
A. Hmm.

577
00:42:21,660 --> 00:42:27,180
This is extraordinary in terms of the continuing return to question.

578
00:42:27,180 --> 00:42:30,540
It seems to me that

579
00:42:32,300 --> 00:42:38,780
it's only in the attitude of the question

580
00:42:38,780 --> 00:42:46,460
that there's any possibility for even intuiting from afar

581
00:42:46,460 --> 00:42:48,220
the possibility of the silence,

582
00:42:48,220 --> 00:42:53,660
since already the answer is a noise.

583
00:42:53,660 --> 00:42:58,140
K. So, sir, just a minute, there's something very interesting.

584
00:43:00,380 --> 00:43:04,620
Does this come up out through questioning?

585
00:43:05,580 --> 00:43:10,220
A. No, I didn't mean to suggest that questioning generates it.

586
00:43:10,220 --> 00:43:16,380
I meant that simply to take a step back

587
00:43:16,380 --> 00:43:22,060
from the enthrallment and enchantment with answers

588
00:43:22,060 --> 00:43:24,940
is in itself a necessary step.

589
00:43:24,940 --> 00:43:28,220
And that in itself has its own terror.

590
00:43:28,220 --> 00:43:31,420
K. Of course, of course. But I'm asking,

591
00:43:31,580 --> 00:43:37,340
is silence, is this sense of immeasurable,

592
00:43:37,340 --> 00:43:41,020
does that come about by my questioning?

593
00:43:41,020 --> 00:43:43,020
A. No.

594
00:43:43,020 --> 00:43:45,020
No.

595
00:43:46,540 --> 00:43:53,660
K. Perception sees the false and discards the false.

596
00:43:55,420 --> 00:43:59,820
There is no question. It sees and it's finished.

597
00:44:01,980 --> 00:44:08,060
But if I keep on questioning, I keep on doubting.

598
00:44:08,060 --> 00:44:13,820
Doubt has its place, but it must be kept on a leash.

599
00:44:15,260 --> 00:44:19,660
A. Now, let me ask you a question here, if I may.

600
00:44:23,900 --> 00:44:28,060
The act of perceiving

601
00:44:28,060 --> 00:44:31,180
is, as you've said, the doing.

602
00:44:31,180 --> 00:44:33,180
K. Absolutely.

603
00:44:33,180 --> 00:44:35,180
A. There's absolutely no interval between one...

604
00:44:35,180 --> 00:44:37,180
K. Sir, I see danger to the act.

605
00:44:37,180 --> 00:44:39,180
A. ...and I act. Exactly.

606
00:44:41,180 --> 00:44:45,980
Now, in this perceiving,

607
00:44:47,900 --> 00:44:51,980
the act is totally free,

608
00:44:51,980 --> 00:44:53,980
K. Yes, sir.

609
00:44:54,780 --> 00:45:02,460
A. And then every energy pattern is free to become change.

610
00:45:02,460 --> 00:45:03,900
K. Yes, quite right.

611
00:45:03,900 --> 00:45:08,940
A. Yes, exactly. No more hoarding to itself

612
00:45:08,940 --> 00:45:12,940
all that it's worked for all its life.

613
00:45:15,100 --> 00:45:17,900
And amazingly though, it seems to me,

614
00:45:17,900 --> 00:45:20,860
if I've understood you correctly, there's a corollary to this.

615
00:45:20,860 --> 00:45:24,780
Not only is the pattern free to be changed,

616
00:45:24,780 --> 00:45:28,060
but the energy is free to pattern itself.

617
00:45:28,060 --> 00:45:31,660
K. Or not to pattern. A. Or not to pattern.

618
00:45:31,660 --> 00:45:35,180
K. Yes. There it is, and the knowledge has to pattern.

619
00:45:35,180 --> 00:45:35,980
A. Of course.

620
00:45:35,980 --> 00:45:38,220
K. But here it can't pattern.

621
00:45:38,220 --> 00:45:41,500
Pattern for what?

622
00:45:42,380 --> 00:45:47,180
If it patterns, it becomes thought again.

623
00:45:47,740 --> 00:45:49,580
And therefore thought is divisive,

624
00:45:49,580 --> 00:45:54,300
thought is superficial.

625
00:45:54,300 --> 00:45:55,660
I don't know if I told you the other day,

626
00:45:55,660 --> 00:45:58,940
somebody was telling me,

627
00:45:58,940 --> 00:46:00,460
Professor Bohmray, in fact,

628
00:46:00,460 --> 00:46:04,540
he was saying that in Eskimo language,

629
00:46:04,540 --> 00:46:08,140
thought means the outside.

630
00:46:10,620 --> 00:46:12,780
Very interesting.

631
00:46:12,780 --> 00:46:14,940
The outside, when you say, go outside,

632
00:46:14,940 --> 00:46:18,140
the word is thought.

633
00:46:20,300 --> 00:46:24,780
So thought has created the outer and the inner.

634
00:46:24,780 --> 00:46:26,860
If thought is not,

635
00:46:26,860 --> 00:46:31,180
then there is neither the outer nor the inner.

636
00:46:31,660 --> 00:46:34,460
That is space.

637
00:46:38,220 --> 00:46:41,340
It isn't I've got inner space.

638
00:46:41,340 --> 00:46:43,580
A. No.

639
00:46:43,580 --> 00:46:45,660
We've been talking about meditation

640
00:46:45,660 --> 00:46:48,380
in relation to religion,

641
00:46:48,380 --> 00:46:53,820
and I simply feel I must ask you

642
00:46:53,820 --> 00:47:00,700
to speak about the interrelationship of prayer

643
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:02,620
to meditation, with meditation,

644
00:47:02,620 --> 00:47:05,420
because conventionally we always refer

645
00:47:05,420 --> 00:47:07,500
to prayer and meditation as...

646
00:47:07,500 --> 00:47:11,900
K. Prayer is no place in meditation.

647
00:47:12,620 --> 00:47:14,940
To whom am I praying?

648
00:47:14,940 --> 00:47:21,180
Whom am I supplicating, begging, asking?

649
00:47:21,980 --> 00:47:26,380
A. Prayer as petition has no place in it.

650
00:47:26,380 --> 00:47:31,500
Is there any use of the word prayer

651
00:47:31,500 --> 00:47:39,500
that would be consonant with what we've been talking about?

652
00:47:40,060 --> 00:47:43,660
If there is no petition,

653
00:47:44,300 --> 00:47:47,820
you understand? Deeply, inwardly, there is no petition.

654
00:47:47,820 --> 00:47:49,660
No grabbing, grasping.

655
00:47:49,660 --> 00:47:52,140
K. Because the grabber is the grabbed.

656
00:47:52,140 --> 00:47:54,540
A. Exactly.

657
00:47:54,540 --> 00:47:58,940
K. If there is no petition, what takes place?

658
00:47:58,940 --> 00:48:02,380
I petition only when I don't understand,

659
00:48:02,380 --> 00:48:04,780
when I'm in conflict, when I'm in sorrow,

660
00:48:04,780 --> 00:48:08,460
when I'm saying, oh God, I've lost everything,

661
00:48:08,460 --> 00:48:13,340
I'm finished, I can't arrive, I can't achieve.

662
00:48:13,340 --> 00:48:16,860
A. When there is no petition I can look.

663
00:48:16,860 --> 00:48:20,060
Yes, exactly.

664
00:48:20,060 --> 00:48:22,380
I can look.

665
00:48:22,380 --> 00:48:26,060
When there is no petition I can look.

666
00:48:26,060 --> 00:48:29,500
Yes, exactly. Exactly.

667
00:48:29,500 --> 00:48:32,940
K. I mean, a woman comes to me once, some time ago,

668
00:48:32,940 --> 00:48:36,460
she said, I have prayed, enormous, for years,

669
00:48:36,460 --> 00:48:41,740
and I prayed for my refrigerator and I've got it.

670
00:48:41,740 --> 00:48:45,020
Yes, sir.

671
00:48:47,260 --> 00:48:49,020
I pray for peace,

672
00:48:49,020 --> 00:48:54,460
and I live a life of violence all the time.

673
00:48:58,140 --> 00:49:01,580
I say, I pray for my country,

674
00:49:01,580 --> 00:49:06,540
and I've divided the country, opposed to another country,

675
00:49:06,540 --> 00:49:09,580
and I pray for my country.

676
00:49:09,580 --> 00:49:13,180
It becomes so childish.

677
00:49:13,180 --> 00:49:15,660
A. In conventional prayers,

678
00:49:15,660 --> 00:49:19,820
there is usually both petition and praise.

679
00:49:19,820 --> 00:49:21,300
Both are there.

680
00:49:21,300 --> 00:49:25,500
K. Of course. Praising and receiving.

681
00:49:25,500 --> 00:49:26,580
A. And of course...

682
00:49:26,580 --> 00:49:27,980
K. You must know in Sanskrit,

683
00:49:27,980 --> 00:49:31,980
it always begins, some parts of it, praising,

684
00:49:31,980 --> 00:49:33,820
and then begging.

685
00:49:33,820 --> 00:49:36,820
A. Yes.

686
00:49:36,820 --> 00:49:39,340
K. There is a marvellous chant,

687
00:49:39,340 --> 00:49:44,900
which is asking protection of the gods.

688
00:49:44,900 --> 00:49:51,140
Protection. And they say, may you protect my steps.

689
00:49:51,140 --> 00:49:52,340
A. Yes.

690
00:49:52,340 --> 00:49:57,780
K. Praising God, then saying, please protect my steps.

691
00:49:57,780 --> 00:50:02,180
So, if there is no petition,

692
00:50:02,180 --> 00:50:07,140
because the petitioner is the petitioner,

693
00:50:07,140 --> 00:50:12,780
the beggar is the beggar, is the receiver,

694
00:50:12,780 --> 00:50:17,500
then what takes place in the mind?

695
00:50:17,500 --> 00:50:21,900
No asking.

696
00:50:21,900 --> 00:50:27,380
A. Immense quietude.

697
00:50:27,380 --> 00:50:34,260
The proper sense of whatever the word tranquillity points to.

698
00:50:34,260 --> 00:50:36,620
K. That is real peace.

699
00:50:36,620 --> 00:50:39,220
Not the funny peace they are all talking about,

700
00:50:39,220 --> 00:50:41,220
politicians and the religious people.

701
00:50:41,220 --> 00:50:46,660
That is real. No asking. Yes. Think.

702
00:50:46,660 --> 00:50:50,860
A. There is a very beautiful biblical phrase,

703
00:50:50,860 --> 00:50:55,060
the peace that passeth understanding.

704
00:50:55,060 --> 00:51:00,740
K. I have heard that phrase when I was a small boy.

705
00:51:03,380 --> 00:51:08,540
A. I have always asked myself since a child,

706
00:51:08,540 --> 00:51:16,300
how it is the case that there is so much talk about such a thing,

707
00:51:16,300 --> 00:51:19,540
and there is so little evidence of it.

708
00:51:19,540 --> 00:51:22,580
K. Sir, I think, you know,

709
00:51:22,580 --> 00:51:27,660
books have become tremendously important.

710
00:51:29,620 --> 00:51:32,260
What they have written, what they have said.

711
00:51:32,260 --> 00:51:37,980
And so the human mind has become second-hand.

712
00:51:40,580 --> 00:51:43,420
Or the mind that has acquired so much knowledge

713
00:51:43,420 --> 00:51:47,380
about what other people have experienced about reality.

714
00:51:47,380 --> 00:51:50,660
How can such a mind experience,

715
00:51:50,660 --> 00:51:56,180
or find, or come upon that thing which is original?

716
00:51:58,860 --> 00:52:01,620
A. Not that route. K. No, sir.

717
00:52:01,620 --> 00:52:07,300
A. And can the mind empty itself of its content?

718
00:52:07,300 --> 00:52:09,780
If it cannot, it cannot.

719
00:52:09,780 --> 00:52:14,380
Acquire, then reject, then receive. You follow?

720
00:52:14,380 --> 00:52:15,500
A. Yes.

721
00:52:15,500 --> 00:52:19,300
K. Why should I go through all those stages?

722
00:52:21,940 --> 00:52:25,620
Why can't I say, well, I'll look.

723
00:52:25,620 --> 00:52:29,020
There is no book in the world that is going to teach me.

724
00:52:29,020 --> 00:52:30,980
There is no teacher that is going to teach me,

725
00:52:30,980 --> 00:52:35,220
because the teacher is the taught.

726
00:52:35,220 --> 00:52:38,780
The disciple is the teacher. I don't know.

727
00:52:38,780 --> 00:52:43,220
A. No, that is in itself, as a statement,

728
00:52:43,220 --> 00:52:50,780
if one will, as we said in an earlier conversation,

729
00:52:50,780 --> 00:52:52,940
at the inception of looking,

730
00:52:52,940 --> 00:52:59,780
if he will hold that very statement,

731
00:52:59,780 --> 00:53:02,700
I am the world and the world is me,

732
00:53:02,700 --> 00:53:06,980
thus is an occasion for healing.

733
00:53:06,980 --> 00:53:11,380
But that very statement, I am the world and the world is me,

734
00:53:11,380 --> 00:53:16,140
sounds, as you have said so often, so absurd,

735
00:53:16,140 --> 00:53:23,580
that at that point one starts to bolt again, panic again.

736
00:53:23,580 --> 00:53:28,420
Meditation, when undertaken,

737
00:53:28,420 --> 00:53:31,420
as it must be, continuously,

738
00:53:31,420 --> 00:53:33,420
because we are talking about that movement.

739
00:53:33,420 --> 00:53:36,260
K. That means one has to be very, very serious.

740
00:53:36,260 --> 00:53:38,780
It isn't a thing that you play with.

741
00:53:38,780 --> 00:53:43,780
A. No. It is not what is called these days a fun thing.

742
00:53:43,780 --> 00:53:47,500
In no sense.

743
00:53:47,500 --> 00:53:52,700
No, no, no, no.

744
00:53:52,700 --> 00:53:59,420
The discussion that you have undertaken concerning it

745
00:53:59,420 --> 00:54:03,500
is so total.

746
00:54:03,500 --> 00:54:07,700
And meditation isn't a thing that you do, among other things.

747
00:54:07,700 --> 00:54:12,540
K. Oh, for Christ's sake. A. No.

748
00:54:12,540 --> 00:54:20,460
K. That is, sir, meditation means attention, care.

749
00:54:20,460 --> 00:54:23,700
That is part of it. Care for my children, for my neighbour,

750
00:54:23,700 --> 00:54:30,060
for my country, for the earth, for the trees, for the animals.

751
00:54:30,060 --> 00:54:32,380
Don't kill animals. You follow?

752
00:54:32,380 --> 00:54:36,140
Don't kill them to eat. It is so unnecessary.

753
00:54:36,140 --> 00:54:44,060
It is part of your... the tradition says, you must eat meat.

754
00:54:44,940 --> 00:54:49,500
Therefore, sir, all this comes to me

755
00:54:49,500 --> 00:54:54,540
as a sense of deep inward seriousness.

756
00:54:54,540 --> 00:55:00,420
And that seriousness itself brings about attention, care,

757
00:55:00,420 --> 00:55:04,060
and responsibility, and all that we discussed.

758
00:55:04,060 --> 00:55:07,580
It isn't that one has gone through all this.

759
00:55:07,580 --> 00:55:10,740
One sees it.

760
00:55:10,740 --> 00:55:15,740
And the very perception is action, which is wisdom.

761
00:55:15,740 --> 00:55:17,620
Right?

762
00:55:17,620 --> 00:55:24,940
Because wisdom is the ending of suffering.

763
00:55:26,220 --> 00:55:31,820
It isn't callousness, it is the ending of it.

764
00:55:32,540 --> 00:55:39,380
And the ending of it means the observation,

765
00:55:39,380 --> 00:55:41,220
the seeing of suffering,

766
00:55:41,220 --> 00:55:44,140
not to go beyond it, refuse it,

767
00:55:44,140 --> 00:55:47,300
rationalise it, or run away from it, just to see it,

768
00:55:47,300 --> 00:55:51,260
let it flower.

769
00:55:51,260 --> 00:55:56,500
And as you are choicelessly aware of this flowering,

770
00:55:56,500 --> 00:56:00,900
it comes naturally to wither away.

771
00:56:00,900 --> 00:56:05,180
I don't have to do something about it.

772
00:56:07,660 --> 00:56:14,140
A.M. – marvelous, marvelous, how energy can be free

773
00:56:14,140 --> 00:56:18,020
to pattern itself, or not pattern itself.

774
00:56:18,020 --> 00:56:21,460
The pattern is free to be energised,

775
00:56:21,460 --> 00:56:29,060
or the whole thing is simply all round.

776
00:56:29,060 --> 00:56:33,380
Yes, sir, it covers the whole of man's endeavour,

777
00:56:33,380 --> 00:56:38,500
his thoughts, his anxiety, everything it covers.

778
00:56:38,500 --> 00:56:43,100
A.M. – so in our conversations all through,

779
00:56:43,100 --> 00:56:47,140
we have reached a point of consummation here,

780
00:56:47,140 --> 00:56:52,940
where it is round.

781
00:56:52,940 --> 00:57:01,980
A.M. – I wonder if Shakespeare had some intimation of this

782
00:57:01,980 --> 00:57:05,780
when he said, ripeness is all.

783
00:57:05,780 --> 00:57:07,540
He must have been thinking of that

784
00:57:07,540 --> 00:57:12,420
not simply as setting a term for the career of a fruit.

785
00:57:12,420 --> 00:57:18,700
K.P. – No, sir, time comes to an end, time stops.

786
00:57:18,860 --> 00:57:22,980
In silence, time stops.

787
00:57:22,980 --> 00:57:27,380
A.M. – In silence, time stops.

788
00:57:27,380 --> 00:57:30,260
K.P. – Good.

789
00:57:30,260 --> 00:57:33,580
A.M. – Immensely beautiful.

790
00:57:33,580 --> 00:57:42,460
I must express to you my gratitude from the bottom of my heart.

791
00:57:42,460 --> 00:57:45,100
I hope you will let me,

792
00:57:45,180 --> 00:57:53,260
because throughout the whole career of our discussions

793
00:57:53,260 --> 00:57:57,660
I have been undergoing a transformation.

794
00:57:57,660 --> 00:57:59,780
K.P. – Because you are willing enough to listen,

795
00:57:59,780 --> 00:58:01,260
good enough to listen.

796
00:58:01,260 --> 00:58:05,300
Most people, they won't listen.

797
00:58:05,300 --> 00:58:12,540
You took the time, the trouble, the care to listen.

798
00:58:12,540 --> 00:58:18,260
I have already seen in my relation to my classes,

799
00:58:18,260 --> 00:58:22,780
in the activity my students and I share,

800
00:58:22,780 --> 00:58:25,700
the beginning of a flowering.

801
00:58:25,700 --> 00:58:29,660
The beginning of a flowering.

802
00:58:29,660 --> 00:58:34,140
Thank you so much again. Thank you.
